@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 A printer that calls print() on a string property, or on a missing property that is not a child key, rejects with the non-node error; a printer without getVisitorKeys is checked against the node's own keys (tests/integration/__tests__/print-pre-check.js) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 print() on a missing property that is a child key prints nothing (tests/integration/__tests__/print-pre-check.js) [AC-2]
+- [ ] 1.3 TypeScript abstract class properties and GraphQL definitions and extensions format unchanged with the check on (tests/integration/__tests__/print-pre-check.js) [AC-3]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Run the check in mainPrintInternal for every printer, before the empty-value return, against printer.getVisitorKeys or the node's own keys; a no-op in production (src/main/create-print-pre-check-function.js, src/main/ast-to-doc.js)
+- [ ] 2.2 Remove the per-language checks (src/language-{css,graphql,handlebars,html,markdown,yaml}/printer-*.js, src/language-js/printer-estree.js)
+- [ ] 2.3 Stop the built-in printers calling print() on keys their nodes do not have (src/language-graphql/printer-graphql.js, src/language-js/print/assignment.js, src/language-js/print/class.js)
+- [ ] 2.4 Throw for a node type with no visitor keys in every build (src/utils/create-get-visitor-keys.js)
